# CLI workflows

The TypeScript SDK ships a small command line tool with two commands. `login` signs you in through your browser and saves an API key for the current folder. `doctor` checks your setup and sends one test trace. Both need Node 18 or newer.

Run them with `npx`:

```bash
npx @uncoil.dev/sdk login
npx @uncoil.dev/sdk doctor
```

If you give no command, `doctor` runs. Use `-h` or `--help` to print the usage text.

## Sign in with login

`login` opens a page in your browser, waits for you to confirm, and then writes the key to an env file. The key is never printed to the terminal.

```bash
npx @uncoil.dev/sdk login --region us
```

The command prints an address and a short code. It also tries to open the address for you. Confirm the code in the browser and the command finishes:

```text
Open this page to sign in: <sign-in address>
Code: <short code>
Waiting for you to confirm in the browser…
Connected to project "Support agent" (US). Key saved to .env.local.
```

The file gets the API key and the project id. It also gets the region when you choose `us`. Other lines in the file stay as they were. The file is created with owner-only permissions. If the folder is a git repository and the file is not already ignored, the command adds its name to `.gitignore`.

| Option | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `--region <eu\|us>` | Data region. Defaults to `UNCOIL_REGION`, then `eu`. |
| `--new <name>` | Create a new project with this name instead of picking one in the browser. |
| `--no-browser` | Print the address and code, but do not open a browser. |
| `--env-file <path>` | Where to save the key. Defaults to `.env.local`. |
| `--host <url>` | Use a custom host. Defaults to `UNCOIL_HOST`. |
| `--json` | Print one JSON object per line instead of text. |

With `--json`, each line has an `event` field: `waiting`, `connected` or `error`. Errors go to stderr. Use `--no-browser` in remote shells and CI.

The command waits until the code expires, plus two minutes, before it gives up.

## Check your setup with doctor

`doctor` runs its checks in order and stops at the first one that fails. It reads `.env.local` and `.env` in the current folder, but values already in your environment win.

```bash
npx @uncoil.dev/sdk doctor
```

```text
Uncoil setup check

✓ Runtime: Node 22.11.0
✓ API key: Found uncoil_sk_live_e…ab12
✓ Region and host: EU · https://eu.cloud.uncoil.dev
✓ Network: Reached https://eu.cloud.uncoil.dev (HTTP 200).
✓ Project: Traces will land in: Support agent
✓ Test trace: Accepted. Look for "Uncoil setup check" (run doctor_…) in your dashboard.

All good. Your setup is ready to send traces.
```

The checks are runtime, API key, region and host, network, project and test trace. The project check only shows when the server can say which project the key belongs to. A marker shows each result: `✓` passed, `✗` failed, `-` skipped. Failed checks add a `Fix:` line.

| Option | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `--key <key>` | API key. Defaults to `UNCOIL_API_KEY`. |
| `--region <eu\|us>` | Data region. Defaults to `UNCOIL_REGION`, then the region in the key. |
| `--host <url>` | Use a custom host. Defaults to `UNCOIL_HOST`. |
| `--no-send` | Skip the test trace. |
| `--json` | Print the report as JSON with `ok`, `host`, `checks` and, after a sent trace, `runId`. |

The test trace is named "Uncoil setup check" and is tagged `uncoil-doctor`. Search for the run id in your dashboard. Use `--no-send` if you do not want it to appear.

## Exit codes

- `0`: the command succeeded. For `doctor`, no check failed.
- `1`: `login` did not finish, or a `doctor` check failed.
- `2`: the options were wrong, such as an unknown option, a missing value, or a region other than `eu` or `us`.

## Common errors

- **No API key was found.** Set `UNCOIL_API_KEY`, pass `--key`, or run `login`.
- **The key does not look like an Uncoil key.** Keys start with `uncoil_sk_`. Copy the key again from the API keys page.
- **The host is not a valid web address.** Use a full address with `https://`, or drop `--host` and use `--region`.
- **The key belongs to one region, but the host points at another.** Pass the matching `--region`, or create a key in the other region.
- **Could not reach the host.** Check your connection, firewall and `--host`. Node's `fetch` does not use `HTTPS_PROXY` on its own, so a proxy may block the request.
- **The project id points at a different project than the key.** Run `login` again in this folder so the key and project are saved together.
- **Rejected with 401 or 403.** The key is wrong, revoked, or from another region. Create a new key.
- **Not accepted with 402 or 429.** You may be over your plan limit or sending too fast. Check [plans and limits](/docs/plans-and-limits).
- **Uncoil had a problem on its side (5xx).** Your app is not affected. Check the status page and try again in a minute.
- **The sign-in code expired, or sign-in was cancelled.** Run `login` again.
- **Too many sign-in attempts.** Wait a few minutes and try again.
- **Timed out waiting for the browser, or could not read the key Uncoil sent.** Run `login` again.
- **Uncoil login needs Node 18 or newer.** Upgrade Node; `doctor` reports the same problem as a failed runtime check.

For more help, see [Troubleshoot your first trace](/docs/troubleshooting) and [Choose an Uncoil Cloud region](/docs/data-regions).
